The first thing to wish for (only if you don't have it already, of course):
a very good weapon, preferably a blessed +2 Stormbringer or Mjollnir.
I prefer Mjollnir because the electrical damage is higher and works 
against undead as well. The only thing with electrical resistance are
energy vortices and blue dragons. All undeads and demons are resistant to the
level drain of Stormbringer.
Don't wish for Excalibur, you can always get it by dipping a long sword into
a fountain.
Wish for a weapon before armor, most monsters on deeper levels can beat you
even with AC0 to -10, nothing is more worse than beeing unable to hit a 
monster that beats you up.
Remember, don't hit acid blobs with Mjollnir and Stormbringer, they aren't
rust free. (So, get Excalibur for that)

Second: Wish for good armor. Gray dragon scale mail +2 works well, if you have
it or are AC -5 or better and have something like shield of reflection,
cloak of magic resistance or a wand of polymorph, wish for gauntlets of
dexterity +2. Your Chance to hit depends on dexterity, not on strength.
(Strength accounts for damage).

IF you have weapon and armor :
wish for a wand of polymorph, polypiling is always the best way of getting 
equipment and mostly save when salvaging the upper levels you've explored
before.

When wishing with a wand of wishing: 
WISH FOR 3 BLESSED SCROLLS OF CHARGING FIRST
The wish is only lost when your luck is so low that the scrolls are cursed.
Otherwise, when the scrolls are uncursed, you regain that wish by charging
the wand. Caution: Charging wands of wishing works only once.
When the wnad has n wishes (n between 1 and 3), you get n-1 +3 +1 wishes 
from the wand instead of n + 1. (n-1 from the wand, 3 from the recharged wand 
and the wand last spell from every wand, just try long enough).

I you have everything else (Wands, Weapons,Armor)
Useful are : Amulets of live saving, blessed potions of gain ability
(userful for bringing up dexterity and all other characteristics)
and magic markers.
Magic Marker (several blessed, at least one cursed and perhaps one uncursed)
are good for writing any kind of scroll, especially cursed and blessed scrolls
of genocide (The cursed ones for wraithes (levels), tengus (teleport and tele
port control) and (seldom) dragons (intrinsincs or armor)), scrolls of 
enchanting weapons and armor (read some confused to make items rust proof)
Retain all these junk scrolls for this purpose, if you have boots of water
walking and a pool of water, dip the scrolls there, the pool does not disappear.

Don't wish for rings of teleport control, you get this intrinsic by eating
tengus and nymphs.

One word to armor : My favorite Armoring are
Blessed Hawaiian shirt (enchanted later)
Blesed gary dragon scale mail (magic resistance)
Shield of reflection
Gauntlets of dexterity (enchanted to a least +5)
boots of water walking (not levitaion, you can't pick things up)
Leather Hat or (if rust proof) Helm of brilliance
Cloak of displacement (works best when invisible)

Except the Helm of Brilliance, all items are rust proof, the wizard can see
invisible objects, but he IS fooled by displacement and the gray dragon
scale mail protects from the touch of death)

Other useful items (I prefer to get by polypiling when I don't have them 
already)
Potions of confusion, long sword (Excailbur), bag of holding, ring of
conflict (VERY useful when the wizards minions show up)

